WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.304 --> 00:00:04.720
ROWAN FLAD: My name is Rowan Flad.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.620
I'm a faculty member in the
anthropology department here.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.824
And I work on archeology in China.

00:00:09.824 --> 00:00:12.240
And so what I'm going to tell
you a little bit about today

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:18.450
is a prediction method, a divination
process, that was used in early China.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:23.070
In particular, I'm going to be talking
about a period in Chinese history

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:27.870
at the beginning of the dynastic
cycle, so about 3,500 years ago.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.740
And associated with a dynasty
called the Shang Dynasty.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.820
Have any of you ever heard
of the term oracle bones?

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.040
Oracle bones often
bring to mind writing.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:42.300
And the reason for that is that
the first inscriptions known

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.060
from China, first writing we
know from Chinese contacts

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:50.670
and the first historical documents
we have, come from bones like these.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.400
And so the documents
that we have, that mark

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.940
the beginning of the
historical record in China,

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.840
are divination records
for the most part.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:08.520
And they are records that document
a series of questions or issues

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:14.640
that the Shang Court wanted to know
more information about from the spirit

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.390
world around them.

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:22.280
Inscriptions were first
identified by an aristocrat that

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.560
lived in the very end of the 19th
century, beginning of the 20th century,

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.270
named Wang Yirong.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:34.500
And he was sick and had
some member of his household

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:40.810
go to the apothecary to get what were
sometimes referred to as dragon bones.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:47.730
These were essentially bones that were
found in an archaeological context that

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:52.560
would then be ground up into
powder and added into medicine.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:58.790
And those powders were thought
to be beneficial to one's health.

00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:02.320
So he sent somebody out, and they
brought back some bones like this one.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.890
And what we have on here
is an inscription that's

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.390
a fragment of a divination record.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:12.390
Wang Yirong recognized
that this was writing

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.360
because he was a scholar himself.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:20.460
He recognized that there were
some similarities to characters

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.410
that he knew from archaic contexts.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:26.460
And he started to compile these,
buy them up from apothecaries all

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:27.130
over the place.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.129
We learned a lot about
the Shang based on these.

00:02:29.129 --> 00:02:31.020
And what we've learned
mostly about is what

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:36.790
the Shang Royalty were most concerned
about, and they were divining about.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:39.960
Each of these divinations,
divination inscriptions,

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.587
has several different sections.

00:02:44.587 --> 00:02:47.670
They don't all have it, but a complete
one has several different sections.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:50.376
It has a date on it,
which is very important.

00:02:50.376 --> 00:02:51.750
Now these are not absolute dates.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:55.170
They are dates in a cycle of 60 days.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.120
So there's a 60-day cycle.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.370
And each of these inscription
when they're complete,

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:02.640
will have two characters
at the beginning of it

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:06.870
that mark the date
within the 60-day cycle.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:11.560
Then they will tell you about who it is
that was responsible for the divining.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.400
And then after that, there's a charge.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:20.280
There's basically a topic about
which the diviners wanted to know.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.660
And then what would
have happened, is you

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:28.231
would have had diviners
who recorded the dates,

00:03:28.231 --> 00:03:31.230
they recorded the topics that they
were divining about, not on the bones

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.290
initially, then they
wait to see what happens,

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:37.950
and then they record the
result. And then all of that

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:41.360
is inscribed onto the
bones in certain cases.

